The main finding: **no real Admin SDK `users.insert` call exists yet.** `createWorkspaceUser` is a dev-only simulation, and nothing passes the admin token to it. The repo has no Gmail sending code, no email library and no password handling. Replacing these is open issue #12.

## 1. Accept flow and call chain

- **UI:** `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/components/review-request.tsx:257` POSTs to `/api/review/requests/${id}/acceptance`.
- **Route:** `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/app/api/review/requests/[id]/acceptance/route.ts`
  - L22 `getReviewAccess(request.headers)` returns `{ status, profile, accessToken }`.
  - L30 `getProvisioningProgress(id, access)`: if this returns something, the request was already accepted, so validation is skipped.
  - L31–39 `getReviewableSignupRequest` checks that status is `verified` and that a `workspaceEmail` exists.
  - L42–48 `getSignupPlan` plus `listManageableGroups(access)`, which re-checks the groups.
  - L49 `isWorkspaceEmailAvailable(access, signup.workspaceEmail)`
  - L53 `acceptSignupRequest(id, access.profile.id)`
  - L56 `provisionAcceptedRequest(id)`. **Only the id is passed, not `access`.**
- **`/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/lib/provisioning.ts`**
  - L24–37 `acceptSignupRequest`: a conditional update from `verified` to `accepted`.
  - L42–69 `provisionAcceptedRequest`: claims `accepted` → `provisioning` with `accountCreateState: "attempting"`, then L53 `createWorkspaceUser(claimed.workspaceEmail)`. Any error sets state to `uncertain`; success sets `created` plus `googleUserId`. It then runs `addUnfinishedMemberships` (L74) and `completeIfAllAdded` (L106), which moves the request to `awaiting_handover`.
- **`/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/lib/directory.ts:88-122`**: the simulated user creation:
```ts
// ponytail: development-only simulation of provisioning writes until #12 replaces them;
// without GOOGLE_SIMULATION they report the Workspace unavailable.
function simulatedDomain() {
  const domain = process.env.GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_DOMAIN;
  if (process.env.GOOGLE_SIMULATION !== "true" || process.env.NODE_ENV === "production" || !domain)
    throw new WorkspaceUnavailable();
  return domain;
}

// The create call may have reached Google even though no answer came back.
export class AccountCreateUncertain extends Error {
  constructor() {
    super("Account creation outcome unknown");
  }
}

// `uncertain.user*` simulates a timeout after the request was sent.
export async function createWorkspaceUser(email: string): Promise<{ id: string }> {
  simulatedDomain();
  if (email.toLowerCase().startsWith("uncertain.user")) throw new AccountCreateUncertain();
  return { id: `sim-user-${email.toLowerCase()}` };
}
```
`addGroupMember(groupId, userId, _role)` at L114 is also simulated. The ids `sim-flaky`, `sim-gone` and `sim-recovering` trigger failures.

Two gaps for a real implementation:
- Neither `provisionAcceptedRequest` nor `retryProvisioning` (L131) receives an `Actor`/token, so one has to be passed through.
- The signup's `givenName`/`familyName` (columns in `src/lib/schema.ts`), which `users.insert` needs, are not passed in.

The `Actor` type is defined at `directory.ts:11`: `{ accessToken: string; profile: { id: string } }`.

## 2. Admin OAuth token

**Scopes** are configured in `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/lib/auth.ts:19-23, 41-51`:
```ts
const requiredScopes = [
  "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/admin.directory.user",
  "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/admin.directory.group",
  "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/admin.directory.rolemanagement.readonly",
] as const;
...
    google: {
      clientId: config.GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID,
      clientSecret: config.GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET,
      hd: config.GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_DOMAIN,
      scope: [...requiredScopes],
      accessType: "offline",
      prompt: "select_account consent",
      includeGrantedScopes: false,
      disableIdTokenSignIn: true,
      overrideUserInfoOnSignIn: true,
```
- L64–75: `getUserInfo` rewrites `account.scope` on every sign-in, because Better Auth does not update it on re-sign-in.
- L91–95: `encryptOAuthTokens: true` and `storeStateStrategy: "database"`.
- L99–100: `idToken` is nulled before it is stored.

**Token retrieval** (`auth.ts:106-135`) uses better-auth's stored account tokens through `auth.api.getAccessToken`:
```ts
export async function getReviewAccess(headers: Headers) {
  ...
    const [account] = await db
      .select()
      .from(schema.account)
      .where(
        and(eq(schema.account.userId, session.user.id), eq(schema.account.providerId, "google")),
      );
    if (!account) throw new WorkspaceUnavailable(true);
    // Grants made before the Directory scopes were widened must be re-consented.
    const granted = (account.scope ?? "").split(/[,\s]+/);
    if (!requiredScopes.every((scope) => granted.includes(scope)))
      throw new WorkspaceUnavailable(true);
    stage = "access-token";
    const token = await auth.api.getAccessToken({ headers, body: { accountId: account.id } });
    if (
      !token.accessToken ||
      (token.accessTokenExpiresAt && new Date(token.accessTokenExpiresAt).getTime() <= Date.now())
    )
      throw new WorkspaceUnavailable(true);
    ...
    return { status: "available", profile, accessToken: token.accessToken } as const;
```
After the token, the function reads the admin's own profile and checks for `GOOGLE_REVIEWER_ROLE_ID` (L131–134).

## 3. Google API helpers

All Google calls use plain `fetch`. Neither `googleapis` nor any Google client library is in `package.json`.

- `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/lib/workspace.ts:41-54`:
```ts
// With `allowMissing`, a 404 is an answer ("not there") rather than a failure.
export async function googleGet(url: string | URL, accessToken: string, allowMissing = false) {
  const response = await fetch(url, {
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}` },
    cache: "no-store",
    signal: AbortSignal.timeout(10_000),
  });
  if (allowMissing && response.status === 404) return null;
  if (!response.ok) {
    await logGoogleFailure(url, response);
    throw new WorkspaceUnavailable(response.status === 401);
  }
  return response.json();
}
```
- `workspace.ts:56-78` `logGoogleFailure`: logs the endpoint with the userKey redacted, the status, and the reasons.
- `workspace.ts:28` `WorkspaceUnavailable(reconnect)`; L80 `readWorkspaceProfile`; L122 `hasReviewerRole`, which has its own fetch loop.
- `directory.ts:13` sets `const directory = "https://admin.googleapis.com/admin/directory/v1"`.
  - L28 is the `pages()` pagination generator.
  - L43 `isWorkspaceEmailAvailable`, L56 `canWriteGroups`, L76 `listManageableGroups`.
- There is no POST helper yet; `googleGet` only does GET.
- **Gmail:** none. ADR 0002 (`docs/adr/0002-admin-oauth-and-approved-profile-changes.md:9`) specifies a separate offline grant for a dedicated mailbox, limited to `gmail.send`.

## 4. Password handling and member email

- **There is no password generation or handling.** ADR 0001 (`docs/adr/0001-google-authoritative-identity-and-profiles.md:7`) says handover "uses the Admin console's existing-user password reset and email flow, with a required password change, rather than emailing a plaintext password." Real `users.insert` requires a `password` field, so a random throwaway value would have to be generated and never stored; that is a design decision to make.
- **Handover is manual.** `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/components/account-handover.tsx:66-91` tells the admin to open the Admin console, choose Reset password, email the instructions, and come back to confirm: "The application never sends or stores the password." `confirmHandover` (`provisioning.ts:198-247`) only records that this happened and captures a reviewer notice.
- **No email is actually sent, and there is no mail library.** Messages are "captured" as rows in the `mailMessage` table (`/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/src/lib/schema.ts:160-169`), gated by `MAIL_CAPTURE=true`:
  - Verification email: `src/app/api/signup/route.ts:42` and `src/app/api/verify/resend/route.ts:39`; the text comes from `src/lib/verification.ts:51`.
  - Rejection: `src/lib/review.ts:82-112` (`captureRejectionNotification`).
  - Reviewer notices to `REVIEWER_NOTIFICATION_GROUP`: `src/lib/review.ts:120-133` (`captureReviewerMail`) and L137 `sendReviewerNotification`.
  - Nothing is sent to the new member on accept.
- The relevant env flags are in `.env.example`: `MAIL_CAPTURE=true`, `GOOGLE_SIMULATION=true`, `REVIEWER_NOTIFICATION_GROUP`, `APP_URL`.

## 5. Test setup

Tests are plain `node:assert/strict` scripts run with `tsx`, plus Playwright for e2e.

**Files:**
- `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/tests/`: `signup.ts`, `workspace.ts`, `review.ts`, `plan.ts`, `provisioning.ts`, `handover.ts`.
- `tests/fake-directory.ts` stubs `globalThis.fetch` for `admin.googleapis.com` (users, groups, roles, roleassignments) using the actor `{ accessToken: "admin-token", profile: { id: "admin-1" } }`. It has no POST/insert handling yet.
- `tests/provisioning.ts:13` sets `GOOGLE_SIMULATION = "true"`. L142–151 cover the uncertain-create case.
- e2e: `tests/review.spec.ts` (accept at L135, uncertain at L186/L279, handover at L299). Config is `playwright.config.ts` with `testMatch: "review.spec.ts"` and baseURL from `E2E_BASE_URL`.

**Commands in `package.json`:**
- `lint`: `oxlint --deny-warnings .`; `lint:fix`: `pnpm lint --fix`
- `format`: `oxfmt --write .`; `format:check`: `oxfmt --check .`
- `test`: `tsx tests/signup.ts && tsx --conditions=react-server tests/workspace.ts && tsx tests/review.ts && tsx --conditions=react-server tests/plan.ts && tsx --conditions=react-server tests/provisioning.ts && tsx --conditions=react-server tests/handover.ts`
- `test:e2e`: `playwright test`
- There is no typecheck script. Use `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit`; `next build` also type-checks.

## 6. Related GitHub issues

- **#12 (OPEN, `ready-for-human`): "Integrate Google provisioning and Gmail delivery".** Parent is #1; blocked by #7, #8, #9, #11. Its acceptance criteria:
  - Real Directory user creation and group memberships through the acting admin, keeping the existing partial/uncertain recovery.
  - Sending through the dedicated mailbox's Gmail grant, with no plaintext passwords.
  - Denied, transport and partial failures keep the safe state and retry actions.
  - A live-tenant smoke check.
- **#11 (CLOSED):** real admin OAuth and Directory reads.
- **Code references:**
  - `directory.ts:88` mentions "until #12 replaces them".
  - `provisioning.ts:41` and `:72` mention #11 for reconciliation, and note the real call must treat "already a member" as success.
- **Other open issues:** #1 (parent epic) and #10 (data expiry).
- **Smoke-check doc:** `/Users/itsmeyaw/projects/binden/docs/live-workspace-smoke-check.md` covers OAuth and reads only, not provisioning.
